    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0495" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg399"/>

                <head>No. 296.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Nelson</hi>,</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 9,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 232.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith, for your information,
                    copies of correspondence between this Department and Senor F. G. Palacio, chargé
                    d’affaires of Mexico at this capital, in regard to alleged furnishing of
                    re-enforcements and supplies to the insurgents in Mexico from the territory of
                    the United States; also copies of letters upon the same subject to the Treasury
                    and Navy Departments.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>






